> Github allows us to create personal copies of other peoples' repositories.
  We call those copies a "fork" of the original.

> When we fork a repo, we're basically asking Github "Make me my own copy of
  this repo please"

> As with pull request, forking is not a Git feature. The ability to fork is
  implemented by Github

